---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Artist Statement &bull; Alan Woodyard Fine-Art Photography"
  description="Artist statement and photographic background of Alan Woodyard. Maritime traditions, coastal civil geometry, and archival print craftsmanship."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 space-y-12">
    <!-- Artist Header -->
    <div class="space-y-4 border-b border-[#222538] pb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded bg-sky-500/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-sky-400 border border-sky-500/30">
        <span>ARTIST STATEMENT &bull; BIOGRAPHY</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white">
        Alan Woodyard
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-serif italic">
        &ldquo;The ocean and the river are relentless editors of form. What endures on the water is stripped of ornament and shaped purely by wind, tide, and structural stress.&rdquo;
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Statement Body -->
    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">On Maritime Space &amp; Working Waterfronts</h2>
      <p>
        My photography is rooted in maritime environments where human craftsmanship meets natural forces. Growing up around the wooden workboat traditions of the Chesapeake Bay and sailing the choppy coastal reaches of the Gulf of Mexico, I became attuned to the quiet dignity of working hulls, weathered deadrise skiffs, and the high-tension geometry of offshore carbon fiber rigging.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whether tracking an IRC 52 cutter running at 24 knots in offshore swells or watching a 4,000-horsepower pushboat maneuver petrochemical barges through the evening haze of the Houston Ship Channel, my objective is to capture the weight, atmosphere, and light of maritime labor and motion.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">Austin Skylines &amp; Tidal Geometry</h2>
      <p>
        In central Texas, that same eye searches for the convergence of architectural order and moving water. The solitary scull on Lady Bird Lake at dawn cuts through the reflective glass of Austin's skyline, creating a fleeting dialogue between steel geometry and kinetic human rhythm.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">Color Science &amp; Archival Permanence</h2>
      <p>
        Every photograph presented in this archive is calibrated to rigid color-science standards. We work in native ProPhoto RGB and Adobe RGB 1998 color spaces, grading under standard D50/D65 illuminants to guarantee that the print hanging in your gallery or study possesses identical luminosity and tonal depth to the master capture.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not print on disposable paper. All physical releases are produced on 100% cotton Hahnemühle Photo Rag 308gsm, ChromaLuxe direct metal panels, or polished optical acrylic float mounts designed to resist UV degradation for over 100 years.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Gear & Craft Spec Box -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#23273e] bg-[#12131d] p-8 space-y-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-wider font-mono">
        Master Photographic Toolchain
      </h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs text-slate-400">
        <div>
          <strong class="text-slate-200 block">Capture Bodies:</strong>
          Fujifilm GFX 100 II (Medium Format 102MP)<br>
          Leica SL3 &bull; Leica M11 Monochrom<br>
          Hasselblad 907X &amp; CFV 100C
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-slate-200 block">Optics:</strong>
          Fujinon GF 45-100mm f/4 &bull; GF 110mm f/2<br>
          Leica APO-Summicron-M 50mm f/2 ASPH<br>
          Sony FE 70-200mm f/2.8 GM OSS II
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-slate-200 block">Color Calibration:</strong>
          X-Rite ColorChecker Digital SG<br>
          D50 5000K Calibrated Proofing Environment<br>
          Mirrored 0.125" Bleed Pre-Flight Engine
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-slate-200 block">Proofing &amp; Curator Contact:</strong>
          Direct: <a href="mailto:alan@alanwoodyard.photo" class="text-sky-400 hover:underline">alan@alanwoodyard.photo</a><br>
          Lab Proofing: <a href="mailto:printing@alanwoodyard.photo" class="text-sky-400 hover:underline">printing@alanwoodyard.photo</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
